\details{
Wraps the ESPN core-v2 endpoint
\code{events/{game_id}/competitions/{game_id}/competitors/{team_id}/statistics}.
This wrapper reads the teams list for the game and fetches the
statistics resource for \strong{both} teams, flattening the nested
\code{splits -> categories -> stats} tree into one long frame: one row per
(team x category x stat). The long shape absorbs ESPN's habit of adding
and retiring stat keys across seasons. Pivot wider with
\code{\link[tidyr:pivot_wider]{tidyr::pivot_wider()}} keyed on \code{stat_name} when a wide team box is wanted.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to the \code{team_id} column -- \code{team_name}, \code{team_abbreviation},
\code{team_location}, \code{team_display_name}, \code{team_short_display_name},
\code{team_nickname}, \code{team_color}, \code{team_alternate_color},
\code{team_logo_href}, and \code{team_logo_dark_href}. A catalog failure degrades
to \code{NA}
rather than erroring the wrapper. Set \code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the
catalog fetch and the join.
